[gd_scene load_steps=4 format=3 uid="uid://unit_animation_3d_transform_tracks"]

; AnimationPlayer driving a plain Node3D (MeshInstance3D) via Godot 4's dedicated
; 3D transform tracks: position_3d, rotation_3d (quaternion) and scale_3d. Unlike
; value tracks (`{ "times": …, "values": … }`), these serialize keys as a flat
; PackedFloat32Array(time, transition, comps…) — stride 5 for position/scale,
; stride 6 for the rotation quaternion. Exercises the flat-keys decoder and the
; QuaternionKeyframeTrack path. Skeletal bone sub-paths (Node:bone) are a separate
; deferred case; this fixture animates a plain node so it renders end-to-end.

